<h2>Implementation Guide: How to Build Your Flywheel</h2>

<p>Reading about the Flywheel is useful. Building it is what matters. Here is a practical implementation guide that breaks the six steps into a 90-day action plan.</p>

<h3>Phase 1: Foundation and Authority (Days 1-30)</h3>

<p>Do not skip this. Do not run ads yet. Do not post on social media yet. Do the foundation work.</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Define your ideal customer.</strong> Write a one-page profile. What do they own? What do they fear? What have their past contractor experiences been? Where do they get information?</li>
<li><strong>Write your positioning statement.</strong> One sentence. Specific. Defensible. Memorize it. Put it on your website. Train your team to say it.</li>
<li><strong>Audit your website.</strong> Test load speed. Test mobile experience. Count your calls-to-action. Fix the leaks.</li>
<li><strong>Optimize your Google Business Profile.</strong> Fill every field. Add 20 photos. Write 5 posts. Answer every question.</li>
<li><strong>Implement a review collection system.</strong> Train your team. Create the QR codes. Set up the follow-up sequence.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Phase 2: Visibility and Capture (Days 31-60)</h3>

<p>Now that your foundation is solid, you can drive traffic without wasting it.</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Create location + service pages.</strong> One page per service per primary location. Minimum 800 words each. Include specific details about that location.</li>
<li><strong>Launch or optimize Google Ads.</strong> Start with a small budget ($1,500-$3,000/month). Focus on high-intent keywords. Send traffic to dedicated landing pages, not your homepage.</li>
<li><strong>Implement click-to-call and lead capture forms.</strong> Test form length. Add social proof near forms. Promise fast follow-up.</li>
<li><strong>Set up the 5-minute response system.</strong> Assign someone. Use notifications. Track response time.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Phase 3: Nurture and Amplify (Days 61-90)</h3>

<p>This is where the flywheel starts spinning on its own.</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Build a 30-day email nurture sequence.</strong> 5-7 emails. Value first. Soft sell at the end.</li>
<li><strong>Set up retargeting ads.</strong> Facebook and Google. Show ads to website visitors who did not convert.</li>
<li><strong>Launch a referral program.</strong> Simple reward. Easy sharing. Promote it at project completion.</li>
<li><strong>Identify 3-5 strategic partners.</strong> Reach out. Propose value exchange. Formalize the relationship.</li>
<li><strong>Measure and iterate.</strong> Track leads by source. Track cost per lead. Track close rate by source. Double down on what works. Cut what does not.</li>
</ol>

